@@ -178,7 +178,7 @@ A stale `apps/web/.next/types` can make `typecheck` fail on a deleted route. Run
   - The remaining BigQuery `items.items_netsuite` reads are the **demand-upload** path (`lib/demand-upload/bq-refs.ts`) and the column probe it uses (`getItemsNetsuiteColumns`). Reporting no longer reads that table: Live Inventory, PO Lead Time, Retail SPS and the wholesale-orders filter all join `getItemMaster()` instead. Live Inventory's old BigQuery join had no `QUALIFY`, so a UPC with two NetSuite items rendered twice with conflicting metadata; the Postgres master's `DISTINCT ON` picks one.
 - **Push reasons are a NetSuite mirror, and the picker is memo sugar.** `supply_push_reasons` mirrors the `CUSTOMLIST_PUSH_REASONS` custom list (`lib/netsuite/sync-push-reasons.ts`, nightly `45 8 * * *` `/api/cron/push-reasons-sync`, also on "Refresh all data"), read through `lib/push-reasons.ts`. Wholesale Comparison's Set Demand Plan modal **requires** one (the memo stays optional beside it) and carries a Sync from NetSuite button, so an empty or stale mirror is self-service rather than a blocked reconcile. The choice is **composed into the memo** — `wholesale accepted - <reason> - <note>` — not stored in a column of its own: the upload pipeline and its BigQuery mirror both pin explicit column lists, and the memo is already what reaches the demand-plan rows and upload history. So reasons are filterable as text, not groupable as a dimension; making them a real dimension means a column through `demand_upload_batches` → `build-rows` → `pg-write` **and** one-off BQ DDL on `demand_plans.current_demand_plan`. The server resolves the label from the mirror by id (`requirePushReasonName`) rather than trusting the posted string. It is **also** stored as its own `demand_upload_batches.push_reason` column, which is what Upload History shows as a Push Reason column — that table is Postgres-only, so a real field there costs a migration and no BQ DDL. The memo keeps its copy **for the BigQuery mirror, not for this app** — a deliberate call, so do not "de-duplicate" it away. `supply_demand_plan.memo` is a plan-authored column retained for mirror fidelity (same category as `forecast_method`): every upload writes it and `plan-push` carries it to `current_demand_plan`, but nothing here reads it — the demand-plan grid's Postgres branch hardcodes `memo: null`, and the `ANY_VALUE(memo)` reader beside it is the BigQuery branch, unreachable unless `PLAN_WRITE_PATH=bq`. So composing the reason into the memo is what puts it in front of Sheets/Looker consumers of the mirror; in-app it is write-only, and Upload History and the variant Activity feed are where a person actually sees it. **A push reason belongs on the change log, never on the plan grid.** It describes one accept, not the pair's current state: keyed to the pair it would label the whole row from whichever accept was newest regardless of the month that accept touched, and a later ordinary upload overwriting the number would not clear it — the column would keep asserting a reason for a figure it no longer explains. It was built on `/demand/demand-plan` and removed for exactly that reason; do not re-add it there. The two correct surfaces are Upload History and the variant's Activity feed. Uploads are audited per BATCH (`demand_plan_upload`) and nothing renders that entity, so accepts never appeared on the variant they changed; `/api/activity` synthesises per-pair upload events (`getUploadEventsForPair`) into the `variant_forecast` feed rather than fanning one upload out into thousands of audit rows. Retired values are flagged `is_inactive`, never deleted, so an old memo still names something real. A custom list is queried as its own table (`FROM CUSTOMLIST_PUSH_REASONS`); `FROM customlist` only enumerates the lists.
 - **Comment threads key on a page id, never a URL.** `comments.page_id` holds a `PAGES` id from `lib/routes.ts`, such as `demand.variant` or `supply.amazon-plan`. `postComment` rejects an unknown id, the thread API reads by it, and the bell and All Comments link and label through `PAGES[id]`. A `PAGES` id is therefore a stored key and is never renamed; a page moves by changing its `path`. `page_url` is the pre-0034 record only, null on new rows, and a legacy row that matched no page keeps a null `page_id` and shows as Unknown page (`docs/adr/0161-comment-page-ids.md`).
-- **Placeholder items (`supply_dev_items`, `DEV-` keys) land only where their Lands in boxes say.** A placeholder's rough plan (channel + qty + months) is written into the demand plan as real rows when saved (`syncRoughDemand`, `lib/dev-items/rough-demand.ts`), so every plan reads the same units — nothing synthesises placeholder demand at read time any more. `in_demand_plan` gates the demand-plan list and Add Missing Demand; `in_supply_plan` / `in_inventory_projection` gate those computes through `lib/supply/dev-item-scope.ts`. Every other reader of `supply_plan_monthly` / `supply_demand_plan` excludes `upc LIKE 'DEV-%'` (Wholesale Comparison, Amazon Plan, `/demand/demand-plan`, the BigQuery push). Placeholder demand is stamped division `shared`, so a new reader that filters `division = ANY([div,'shared'])` must also drop `DEV-` keys or it shows every division's placeholders.
+- **Placeholder items (`supply_dev_items`, `DEV-` keys) land only where their Lands in boxes say.** A placeholder's rough plan (channel + qty + months) is written into the demand plan as real rows when saved (`syncRoughDemand`, `lib/dev-items/rough-demand.ts`), so every plan reads the same units — nothing synthesises placeholder demand at read time any more. `in_demand_plan` gates the demand-plan list, the `/demand/demand-plan` grid and Add Missing Demand; `in_supply_plan` / `in_inventory_projection` gate those computes through `lib/supply/dev-item-scope.ts`. Every other reader of `supply_plan_monthly` / `supply_demand_plan` excludes `upc LIKE 'DEV-%'` (Wholesale Comparison, Amazon Plan, the BigQuery push). Placeholder demand is stamped division `shared`, so a new reader that filters `division = ANY([div,'shared'])` must also drop `DEV-` keys or it shows every division's placeholders.
 - **`Segmentation.sales_channels` is the canonical sales-channel registry** — one definition of "a valid sales channel" for the whole app. Read it through `fetchChannelMeta()` (`lib/demand-upload/bq-refs.ts`, 5-min cached): `validNames` gates demand uploads, `discountMultiplier`/`revenueSource` price the plan, and `refs` gives `{id, name}` from its `netsuite_id` column for anything writing a channel back to NetSuite. Do **not** query `saleschannel` over SuiteQL — the M2M role has no permission on it, and NetSuite reports that as the misleading `Record 'saleschannel' was not found`.
 - **Read a lead time or a default ship method through `loadSupplyLocations(division)`** (`lib/supply/locations.ts`), never a direct select of `supply_locations`: the per-division values live in the `supply_location_divisions` overlay, so a direct select hands every division HydroJug's numbers (ADR 0041).
 - **NetSuite** (`lib/netsuite/client.ts`, OAuth2 JWT M2M): SuiteQL reads + PO creation + vendor-tool sync. Every call goes through the client's `nsFetch` / `nsSuiteQLRows` (rows parsed through a `lib/row-parse.ts` schema) / `nsCreateRecord` / `nsUpdateRecord` / `nsRestletFetch`, and a record create retries only on NetSuite's concurrency block, because a retried 5xx can write a duplicate PO; the client, its retry policy and the read modules are in `docs/adr/0018-netsuite-client-and-reads.md`, and the write modules in `docs/adr/0019-netsuite-writes.md`.
